<h1>Gaming on Apple Silicon</h1>
<p>
  GPU TFLOPS and memory bandwidth are the two numbers that matter most for gaming on Apple Silicon. Ray tracing arrived with M3 and improves each generation. More GPU cores push higher frame rates at higher resolutions, while memory bandwidth determines how fast textures and assets stream in.
</p>

<h2>Laptops</h2>
<p>The M5 Max 40-core GPU tops the laptop lineup at 20.5 TFLOPS and 614 GB/s bandwidth—ideal for AAA titles at native resolution. The M5 Pro is a solid mid-range pick for 1080p–1440p gaming. The base M5 and MacBook Neo's A18 Pro handle casual and older titles well, but lack the bandwidth for demanding games.</p>

